--
-- ICAO reference-data seed (AtroCore / AtroPIM)
--
-- WHY THIS EXISTS
-- ---------------
-- The USOAP citation chain this platform is built around --
-- `UsoapProtocolQuestion` -> cites -> `AcapiteOACI` (an Annex paragraph) ->
-- `Normativa` (a national regulation article, added by each adopting
-- authority) -- has its top two links missing on a fresh install: no ICAO
-- Annex documents, no Annex paragraphs, and no USOAP Protocol Questions
-- exist until this seed runs. `sql/seed-usoap-evidence-expectations.sql`
-- already depends on `usoap_protocol_question` being populated (it resolves
-- each row's parent PQ by `code` via a subquery) and silently resolves every
-- row to a NULL parent without this.
--
-- Unlike `Normativa` (a specific country's national law -- deliberately
-- NOT seeded here; each adopting authority enters its own), everything in
-- this file is ICAO-standard content: the same 15 Annex documents, ~1,890 Annex
-- paragraphs and 281 USOAP Protocol Questions apply to any State running a
-- USOAP-aligned oversight programme. Re-entering this by hand is exactly
-- the kind of tedious, error-prone data-entry task a vanilla install should
-- not require of every adopter.
--
-- SOURCE
-- ------
-- Extracted from a legacy database snapshot that predates this platform's
-- synthetic demo dataset (the source of `sql/seed-nomenclatura-catalog.sql`
-- and `sql/seed-demo-dataset.sql` era work), restricted to `deleted = false`
-- rows whose id does not start with `demo-` -- the demo-only rows
-- (`demo-doc-a10v3`, three `demo-acapite-*` paragraphs, three
-- `demo-pq-*` protocol questions PQ 99.001-003, and their citation links)
-- are already created by `sql/seed-demo-dataset.sql` and are intentionally
-- excluded here to avoid any overlap.
--
-- Row counts (verified against the source on extraction):
--   documento_o_a_c_i (ICAO Annex documents)            15
--   acapite_o_a_c_i (Annex paragraphs)                1,890
--   usoap_protocol_question (USOAP Protocol Questions)   281
--   usoap_protocol_question_acapite_o_a_c_i (citations)  439
--
-- `critical_element` and `area_code` on `usoap_protocol_question` reference
-- the `usoapCriticalElement` / `usoapAreaCode` extensible-enum option ids
-- `sql/seed-usoap-vocabularies.sql` creates -- the ids in this file are the
-- same canonical AtroCore-generated ids that seed was itself built from, so
-- no translation was needed; they resolve correctly as long as that seed
-- has already run (see WHEN TO RUN).
--
-- WHEN TO RUN
-- -----------
-- After the AtroCore schema exists and after the USOAP/risk vocabularies,
-- before the nomenclatura catalog and the demo dataset:
--
--   docker compose up -d
--   ./scripts/install-metadata.sh
--   docker compose exec -u www-data atro-web php /var/www/localhost/console.php clear cache
--   docker compose exec -u www-data atro-web php /var/www/localhost/console.php sql diff --run
--   ./scripts/seed-usoap-vocabularies.sh --yes
--   ./scripts/seed-icao-reference-data.sh --yes
--   ./scripts/seed-nomenclatura.sh --yes
--   ./scripts/seed-demo-dataset.sh --yes
--
-- HOW TO RUN
-- ----------
--   ./scripts/seed-icao-reference-data.sh --yes   (preferred wrapper)
--
-- Or directly:
--   docker compose exec -T db psql -U "$POSTGRES_PIM_USER" -d "$POSTGRES_PIM_DB" \
--     -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 < sql/seed-icao-reference-data.sql
--
-- ADDITIVE and NON-DESTRUCTIVE: it only INSERTs, with ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING,
-- exactly like seed-usoap-vocabularies.sql. It never overwrites a deployment
-- that already has this catalog (or has customised/extended it), and it is
-- deliberately NOT removed by `seed-demo-dataset.sh --remove` -- like the
-- USOAP/risk vocabularies, this is reference infrastructure, not demo data.
--

BEGIN;

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 1. ICAO Annex documents (15)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 2. Annex paragraphs (1,890)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 3. USOAP Protocol Questions (281)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
